From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dixonSolutions <203963471+dixonSolutions@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:06:53 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: gtactive3wifi: kernel: performance fragment

- LRU_GEN + LRU_GEN_ENABLED (multi-gen LRU): less kswapd time and fewer
  working-set refaults under memory pressure on a 4 GB tablet swapping to
  zram (ChromeOS/Android fleet results of the series; Fedora default)
- MQ_IOSCHED_DEADLINE: the block layer then defaults to mq-deadline on the
  single-queue UFS LUNs (elevator_set_default()), so reads are not starved
  by long writes (A/B /usr updates, podman pulls) and I/O priorities apply;
  today only "none" exists
- SCHED_MC: per-cluster scheduler domains (arm64 defconfig) for the A55 and
  M3 clusters; degenerates while only the A55s are online
- PREEMPT_DYNAMIC: preempt=full|lazy on the command line (default lazy, as
  before), to measure full preemption (stock kernel, Android GKI) for
  compositor latency without a rebuild

All four lines survive olddefconfig on cand/1022 (gen-kernel-config.sh).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh               |  2 +-
 .../kernel/performance.config                 | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/performance.config

diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh
index 9c800af..29247bf 100755
--- a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/gen-kernel-config.sh
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ OUTCFG=$APORT/config-postmarketos-exynos9810.aarch64
 LOCK=$ROOT/build/kbuild.lock
 BUILDER=${BUILDER:-gta3-pkgbuilder}
 # device fragments, applied in this order
-DEVFRAGS="gtactive3wifi.config virt.config camera.config pm.config hwgaps.config"
+DEVFRAGS="gtactive3wifi.config virt.config camera.config pm.config hwgaps.config performance.config"
 
 podman image exists "$BUILDER" ||
 	podman build -t "$BUILDER" -f "$HERE/../pkgbuilder.Containerfile" "$HERE/.."
diff --git a/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/performance.config b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/performance.config
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8108e18
--- /dev/null
+++ b/contrib/samsung-gtactive3wifi/kernel/performance.config
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# Responsiveness and memory for the SM-T570: 4 GB RAM swapping to zram,
+# 4 Cortex-A55 now (4 Mongoose M3 later), UFS 2.1. One reason per option.
+
+# Multi-generational LRU: page reclaim that sorts pages into generations by
+# how recently they were used instead of two lists, with less kswapd CPU
+# time and fewer working-set refaults under memory pressure (the series'
+# ChromeOS and Android fleet results: fewer low-memory kills and tab
+# discards; Documentation/admin-guide/mm/multigen_lru.rst). Enabled by
+# default in Fedora's kernels. With zram swap it decides what gets
+# compressed, so the apps in use keep their pages.
+CONFIG_LRU_GEN=y
+CONFIG_LRU_GEN_ENABLED=y
+
+# mq-deadline for the UFS LUNs. With it built in, the block layer picks it
+# by default for single-queue devices (elevator_set_default()); without it
+# only "none" exists. Reads (an app starting, the UI paging in code) get a
+# 500 ms deadline against 5 s for writes, so a long write (an A/B /usr
+# update streams 5 GB, a podman pull) does not starve them, and I/O
+# priorities (ionice, IOSchedulingClass=) take effect. The stock kernel
+# also favours synchronous reads (cfq).
+CONFIG_MQ_IOSCHED_DEADLINE=y
+
+# Scheduler domains per CPU cluster (arm64 defconfig): load balancing and,
+# later, energy-aware placement treat the A55 and M3 clusters (separate
+# caches) as such. With only the A55 cluster online the extra level
+# degenerates and costs nothing.
+CONFIG_SCHED_MC=y
+
+# Preemption model selectable at boot (preempt=full|lazy), default lazy as
+# before: lets the device test full preemption (stock Samsung kernel and
+# Android GKI) for compositor latency without a rebuild.
+CONFIG_PREEMPT_DYNAMIC=y
